id: pm-context-claim-resume
title: Resume an item from the last recorded claim
description: "Return a read-only item brief with current status and net field changes since the selected author’s latest recorded claim, using verified tracker history and bounded, restorable output."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: context,resumption
created_at: "2026-11-19T03:40:28.170Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-19T04:26:27.508Z"
assignee: codex-sol-df
claim_principal: codex-sol-df
author: codex-sol-df
acceptance_criteria: "Real SDK and CLI reads anchor to the exact author’s most recent recorded claim, reconcile history with current item state, and disclose missing or invalid baselines.; Report current state and net changes, preserving new collection entries and replacements, with typed omissions and recovery for budget-deferred changes.; Verify with real tracker tests and a reproducible core-versus-extension token measurement on the public pm-context tracker."
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-19T03:41:13.121Z",codex-sol-df,"Round DF gap analysis against pm-cli 2026.11.18 on public pm-context main at 13a9f0c. Core orient and inspect provide intent projections, token limits and omission receipts. Ranked by removable context in sampled loops: (1) claim-bound resume, 5,985 estimated tokens for compact history plus two projected item reads on pm-context-ci-v2. Existing since packs are tracker-wide and require a timestamp or cursor. (2) adaptive projection selection, 1,901 tokens for inspect plus a targeted field retry on the same item, with 1,127 tokens in the first response. Core fields and task-phase already cover known contracts. (3) cross-tracker linking, 320 tokens for one source projection, tag search and target projection using pm-ops issue 272. Diff-based focus already exists. Counts use the SDK UTF-8 estimate per complete stdout."
  "2026-11-19T03:41:14.347Z",codex-sol-df,"Design: register a typed context-resume command and intent. Select one author’s latest verified claim in one item history stream, then compare the canonical claim snapshot with the current item. Show mandatory current state and lossless whole-field net changes. Use SDK output fitting and omission receipts for deferred work fields, with historical endpoint recovery. Reads do not claim or update the item."
  "2026-11-19T03:53:25.474Z",codex-sol-df,"Public measurement on pm-context main 13a9f0c with pm 2026.11.18 and o200k_base: compact history 1,322 tokens, claim projection 2,466, current projection 2,799, total 6,587. The resume brief used 1,145 tokens and included all five work-field changes, saving 5,442 (82.6%). SDK estimates were 5,985 and 974. The projection-selection sample was 2,195 tokens, with up to 1,338 spent on the preliminary inspect response. The cross-tracker sample was 329 tokens, with 121 spent on resolving the known tag."
  "2026-11-19T03:53:26.185Z",codex-sol-df,"SDK compatibility: 2026.10.27 is the earliest published SDK in the prior peer range exposing the output-envelope fitter. Verified the installed command on this host floor and the measurement host 2026.11.18. The manifest and npm peer floor now declare 2026.10.27."
  "2026-11-19T04:25:36.801Z",codex-sol-df,The first full run found a stale complete command-registry expectation and a release-build fixture that copies only indexed sources. Updated the registry expectation and explicitly staged the new module. The registry and release-build checks pass on re-run.
  "2026-11-19T04:26:27.500Z",codex-sol-df,"The linked typecheck, docstring lint, whitespace check, and regenerated changelog check passed. The initial coverage run reached its 20-minute linked-test timeout. A direct full-depth coverage rerun is in progress on the corrected staged tree."
